          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Retinitis pigmentosa is an inherited genetic disease that causes loss of vision.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 4
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The inheritance of a rare form of retinitis pigmentosa in a family is shown in Fig. 2.1.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 4
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "fig2.1",
            "caption": "Fig. 2.1",
            "src": "figures/q2_fig2_1.png",
            "alt": "Copyright placeholder for the pedigree",
            "source": {
              "qp": 4
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Scientists concluded that the inheritance of this rare form of retinitis pigmentosa is linked to the Y chromosome.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 5
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Using evidence shown in Fig. 2.1, explain why the scientists reached this conclusion.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "marks": 3,
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "16.2(2)",
            "role": "primary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
