          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Incontinentia pigmenti is a disease that affects the skin, hair and central nervous system.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 5
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The disease is caused by a dominant allele on the X chromosome.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 5
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Construct a genetic diagram to determine the expected offspring for a healthy father and a heterozygous mother with incontinentia pigmenti.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 5
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "State the expected phenotypic ratio of the offspring.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 5
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use the symbols: <b>X<sup>A</sup></b> = allele for incontinentia pigmenti <b>X<sup>a</sup></b> = normal allele",
